cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or dataset in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Real-Time Pothole Detection Based on Vision-Dominant Sensor Fusion and Dual ESP32 Architecture"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-03-20"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SanTiwari07/PotHoleDetection"
abstract: >
  An embedded IoT system for real-time pothole detection and severity classification
  using a dual ESP32 architecture, YOLOv8 computer vision, and multi-sensor fusion
  combining GPS coordinates, RTC timestamps, and MPU6050 accelerometer jerk data.
  The system produces geo-tagged severity logs suitable for road-maintenance prioritization.
keywords:
  - pothole detection
  - YOLOv8
  - object detection
  - sensor fusion
  - ESP32
  - IoT
  - road monitoring
  - SORT tracking
  - embedded systems
  - computer vision
